            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0351" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">718.1915/588: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-07T00:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1921—12 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 8—10:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>125. Messenger has just arrived Punta Arenas announcing that Costa Rican forces
                    took peaceable possession of Coto region late afternoon September 5th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
